s 'basic review interaction' (so the paraphrase is traceable), or soften the Problem statement to track the document's own wording ('S7 Task 2 did not pass') instead of the unsupported gloss 'basic review interaction'.","fixability":"assisted","proposedFix":{"rationale":"The equivalence between 'S7 Task 2' and 'basic review interaction' isn't verifiable from the evidence given; a human should pick whether to add a grounding citation for that equivalence or reword the Problem statement to the document's literal terms.","options":["Add a citation to the S7 Task 2 definition (e.g. its LLD/BUILD task description) establishing it tested basic review interaction, then keep the phrase as-is.","Reword the Problem statement to say 'before S7 Task 2 passed' (ROLLBACK.md's own wording) instead of the paraphrase 'basic review interaction'.","Leave as-is and accept the paraphrase as reasonable narrative shorthand (no further action)."]}},{"claimId":"cl13","kind":"inventory","severity":"LOW","premise":"Each story's acceptance criteria cite constraint ids (kN) via '_(operationalizes ...)_', and every kN referenced this way (k1-k8) exists in the section-5 constraints table — no acceptance criterion operationalizes a non-existent constraint id.","evidence":"The 14 acceptance-criteria matches (DEF.md:79-84, 96-99, 111-114) cite exactly the anchors listed (s1/ac1-ac6, s2/ac1-ac4, s3/ac1-ac4). Collecting every `kN` cited across them yields k1,k2,k3,k4,k5,k6,k7,k8 — no id outside that range appears (e.g. s1/ac6 cites k6,k7,k8; s3/ac4 cites k1-k8). The section-5 constraints table (DEF.md:58-65) has exactly 8 rows, `k1` through `k8`, matching the grep count. Every kN referenced by an acceptance criterion resolves to a real row in the table; none is dangling.","action":"none — verified sound","fixability":"manual"},{"claimId":"cl14","kind":"closed-union","severity":"LOW","premise":"The Non-goals section (section 3) enumerates exactly four excluded scopes, each tied to a stated user rationale, and none of the six Stories' acceptance criteria reintroduce those excluded scopes (e.g. no AC performs partial-task checkpointing or HEAD-based scope inference).","evidence":"The bullet-pattern grep over DEF.md returns 10 matches total: lines 30-41 are the six Stories' FRs, and lines 45-48 are exactly four Non-goals bullets, each ending in an em-dash rationale clause (45: rolled-back investigation engine — 'user explicitly requested a fresh, simpler review design'; 46: replacement session-threading framework — 'user identified session-per-thread work in another branch'; 47: uncommitted/HEAD-based/partial-task checkpoints — 'user requires a committed review set, submitted scope and completed-task checkpoints'; 48: replacing design-artifact review / auto-approving builds — 'reuses existing CR and human BUILD approval flow'). This confirms 'exactly four excluded scopes, each tied to a stated user rationale.' The targeted greps for the two excluded-scope keywords named in the premise's own example ('HEAD-based' and 'partial-task checkpoint') were run over the whole DEF.md file (not line-scoped) and each returns only two hits: the Non-goals bullet itself (line 47) plus exactly one AC (ac1 line 79 for HEAD-based, ac4 line 82 for partial-task checkpoint) — and in both cases the AC explicitly REJECTS the excluded behavior ('fails explicitly without a HEAD-based fallback'; 'no partial-task checkpoint is treated as completed work') rather than reintroducing it. No additional, unexpected matches turned up elsewhere in the document, which is the evidence that would have surfaced a violation in any of the other Stories' ACs.","action":"none — verified sound","fixability":"manual"}],"counts":{"high":0,"med":3,"low":11},"reviewedAt":"2026-10-30T18:43:16.510Z","model":"cli-claude:claude-sonnet-5","reviewedBy":"daemon"},"resolutions":{}}}}}
